              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`std::async(fn, args)` returns a ==std::future<T>==",
                "`get()` **blocks** until ready, rethrows the task's exception, works ==once only=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Policy",
                "Runs",
                "When"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "default",
                  "may be **deferred**",
                  "implementation's choice"
                ],
                [
                  "`launch::async`",
                  "new thread",
                  "forced"
                ],
                [
                  "`launch::deferred`",
                  "calling thread",
                  "lazily, on `get()`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Ignored future",
              "text": "A future from `async` ==blocks in its destructor== until the task ends. Discard it and the call is **synchronous**."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. promise and packaged_task",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "std::promise<int> p;",
                "std::future<int> f = p.get_future();",
                "std::thread t([&p]{ p.set_value(42); });",
                "int v = f.get();  // blocks",
                "t.join();"
              ],
              "note": "writer holds the promise, reader holds the future"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`set_value` or `set_exception` sets the result; `get_future()` is the {green:reader side}",
                "`packaged_task` wraps a callable the same way; run it on any thread"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
